## Part 3 — Host tests for the generator

All in-module `#[cfg(test)]` (house style; no crate-level `tests/` dir exists anywhere in the workspace). Live in the measured lib modules so Sonar sees the coverage.

**The D8-mandated layout snapshot** — `ipc_h.rs`:

```rust
#[test]
fn ipc_h_pins_the_live_message_layout() {
    // Snapshots the GENERATED text against Message's own const asserts: the
    // generator must never hardcode 104/8/8, and a Rust-side layout change
    // must show up in the header or fail here.
    let h = render();
    let m = Message { m_source: 0, m_type: 0, payload: [0; 96] };
    let base = &m as *const _ as usize;
    let payload_off = m.payload.as_ptr() as usize - base;

    assert!(h.contains(&format!("sizeof(message) == {}", size_of::<Message>())));
    assert!(h.contains(&format!("_Alignof(message) == {}", align_of::<Message>())));
    assert!(h.contains(&format!("offsetof(message, payload) == {payload_off}")));
    assert_eq!(size_of::<Message>(), 104);   // the ABI number itself, pinned
    assert_eq!(payload_off, 8);
}
```

Rest of the suite:

| Module | Test | What it catches |
|---|---|---|
| `com_h` | `boot_endpoints_match_boot_endpoint_fn` | The `_EP` values are `boot_endpoint(nr)`, computed independently in the test (SYSTEM 32766, HARDWARE 32767, PM 0 …) |
| `com_h` | `negative_proc_numbers_are_parenthesized` | `#define SYSTEM_PROC_NR (-2)` not `-2` |
| `com_h` | `every_proc_has_both_a_proc_nr_and_an_ep` | The pairing invariant |
| `callnr_h` | `kernel_calls_render_from_live_constants` | e.g. text contains `SYS_EXEC 0x603` derived from `callnr::SYS_EXEC` |
| `callnr_h` | `every_band_base_and_count_appears` | Coverage of the five bands |
| `errno_h` | `minix_band_is_error_all_above_the_base` | Driven off `error::ALL` + `MINIX_ERRNO_BASE` |
| `errno_h` | `posix_block_is_not_defined_only_asserted` | `#define EPERM` absent, `_Static_assert(EPERM ==` present |
| `errno_h` | `standin_covers_exactly_the_posix_block` | 40 defines, values from `ALL` |
| `builder` | `guard_open_close_match`, `define_hex_format`, `static_assert_escapes_quotes` | Writer mechanics |
| `lib` | `every_artifact_has_spdx_and_do_not_edit` | Licence header discipline on generated output |
| `lib` | `every_artifact_is_ascii` | No smart quotes / em dashes leaking into musl |
| `lib` | `header_guards_are_unique_across_artifacts` | Two headers sharing a guard silently blanks one |
| `lib` | `no_duplicate_define_names_within_a_header` | Parse `#define NAME`, assert distinct — the real bug class as bands multiply |
| `lib` | `all_define_names_are_c_identifiers` | Catches a Rust name that isn't C-legal |
| `lib` | `artifact_paths_are_relative_and_distinct` | Prevents an escape from OUTDIR |
| `lib` | `rendering_is_deterministic` | `artifacts()` twice → identical bytes |
| `selftest` | `selftest_includes_every_generated_header_twice` | Guard exercise stays wired |

