## Part 2 — `tools/gen-c-headers`

### 2.1 Crate layout

```
tools/gen-c-headers/
├── Cargo.toml
└── src/
    ├── lib.rs        # artifact list + crate docs        (measured)
    ├── builder.rs    # CFile writer: banner/guards/defines/_Static_assert  (measured)
    ├── ipc_h.rs      # minix/ipc.h                        (measured)
    ├── com_h.rs      # minix/com.h                        (measured)
    ├── callnr_h.rs   # minix/callnr.h                     (measured)
    ├── errno_h.rs    # minix/errno.h + musl stand-in      (measured)
    ├── selftest.rs   # abi-selftest.c                     (measured)
    └── main.rs       # argv + fs I/O only        (Sonar coverage-excluded)
```

Lib + thin bin is the house shape (`servers/ds`: `registry.rs` measured, `main.rs` excluded). It also keeps all filesystem I/O out of the test-covered modules, which matters because it leaves the door open to miri later.

**`tools/gen-c-headers/Cargo.toml`** — internal-crate convention (literal fields, `publish = false`, explicit targets). `publish = false` is load-bearing: `release.yml` publishes a hardcoded 5-crate list, so a `publish = true` member would only be a footgun for `cargo package`.

```toml
[package]
name = "minixrs-gen-c-headers"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2024"
license = "BSD-3-Clause"
publish = false

[lib]
name = "minixrs_gen_c_headers"
path = "src/lib.rs"

[[bin]]
name = "minixrs-gen-c-headers"
path = "src/main.rs"

# Zero third-party dependencies on purpose: the argv handling is ten lines, and
# a dep here would have to clear deny.toml's license allow-list, cargo-audit,
# and cargo-geiger for no benefit.
[dependencies]
minixrs-kernel-shared = { path = "../../kernel-shared" }
```

`lib.rs` gets `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` (the `server-rt` precedent) so the advisory geiger sweep is trivially clean.

### 2.2 CLI

```
usage: cargo gen-c-headers [OUTDIR]      # default: target/gen-c-headers
       cargo gen-c-headers --stdout      # concatenate every artifact to stdout
       cargo gen-c-headers --help
```

`main()` returns `std::process::ExitCode` (0 ok, 2 usage, 1 I/O), `fs::create_dir_all`s each artifact's parent, writes, and prints `wrote <path>` per file. `--stdout` satisfies D8's literal "*prints* the C headers" wording and is the eyeball path during development.

**Determinism rule (state it in the crate docs):** no timestamps, no hostname, no absolute paths, no environment reads in generated output. The same commit must produce byte-identical bytes so the 5.6 sysroot cache and any `git diff --exit-code` guard work.

