### 2.3 `builder.rs` — the measured core

A tiny append-only writer, no `std::fmt::Write` (`write!` into a `String` returns a `Result` that clippy makes you handle a hundred times):

```rust
pub struct CFile { out: String }

impl CFile {
    pub fn new(title: &str, sources: &[&str]) -> Self;   // SPDX + copyright + GENERATED banner
    fn line(&mut self, s: &str);                          // push_str + '\n'
    pub fn guard_open(&mut self, guard: &str);            // #ifndef/#define
    pub fn guard_close(&mut self, guard: &str);           // #endif /* guard */
    pub fn section(&mut self, title: &str);
    pub fn block_comment(&mut self, lines: &[&str]);
    pub fn include(&mut self, header: &str, why: &str);   // #include <h>  /* why */
    pub fn define_dec(&mut self, name: &str, v: i64);     // parenthesizes negatives
    pub fn define_hex(&mut self, name: &str, v: i64);
    pub fn define_ep(&mut self, name: &str, v: i32);      // ((endpoint_t) N)
    pub fn static_assert(&mut self, expr: &str, msg: &str);
    pub fn finish(self) -> String;
}
```

Two rules that need tests: `define_dec` must emit `(-2)` not `-2` (otherwise `x-SYSTEM_PROC_NR` mis-parses), and every string must stay **ASCII** (no em dashes / smart quotes leaking into a header that ships into musl).

Shared banner:

```
