## Part 4 — CI wiring

### New job (blocking), inserted after `clippy-kernel` in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`

```yaml
  c-headers:
    name: generated C headers
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    # Blocking (D8): the generated headers are the musl fork's only view of the
    # minix.rs ABI, so a Rust-side change that produces uncompilable C must fail
    # in the slice that made it, not in 5.6 when the first C file appears.
    # `clang` needs no install step -- it ships on the GitHub runner images, and
    # kernel/build.rs already shells out to bare `clang` for the kernel's .S
    # files, so it is an existing hard build requirement (the green qemu-smoke
    # job on ubuntu-24.04-arm is the standing proof).
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@df4cb1c069e1874edd31b4311f1884172cec0e10 # v6.0.3
      - name: Install pinned toolchain
        run: rustup show
      - uses: Swatinem/rust-cache@e18b497796c12c097a38f9edb9d0641fb99eee32 # v2
      - name: Generate headers
        run: cargo gen-c-headers
      # -nostdlibinc (not -nostdinc) keeps the check hermetic while preserving
      # clang's freestanding resource-dir headers (<stddef.h>): the selftest can
      # then see ONLY the generated headers, so it cannot accidentally validate
      # against the host libc -- whose errno values differ from musl's (Darwin
      # EDEADLK is 11, not 35). Two triples: the host proves portability, the
      # aarch64-musl triple is the ABI that actually ships. -fsyntax-only needs
      # no backend and no sysroot.
      - name: Syntax-check the generated headers
        run: |
          for target in "" "--target=aarch64-unknown-linux-musl"; do
            clang -std=c11 -pedantic-errors -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
              -fsyntax-only -nostdlibinc $target \
              -Itarget/gen-c-headers/include \
              target/gen-c-headers/abi-selftest.c
          done
      # Compiles <minix/errno.h>'s guarded POSIX block against the generated
      # stand-in. A syntax + name-spelling check only (the stand-in comes from
      # the same Rust table); the value check lands with the musl sysroot in 5.6.
      - name: Syntax-check the guarded errno assertions
        run: |
          clang -std=c11 -pedantic-errors -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
            -fsyntax-only -nostdlibinc -DMINIX_ABI_CHECK_POSIX_ERRNO \
            -Itarget/gen-c-headers/abi-check \
            -Itarget/gen-c-headers/include \
            target/gen-c-headers/abi-selftest.c
      # D8: headers are build artifacts under target/ and are NEVER committed.
      - name: Assert nothing was written into the tree
        run: git diff --exit-code && git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all
```

