## Part 4 — CI wiring

### New job (blocking), inserted after `clippy-kernel` in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`

```yaml
  c-headers:
    name: generated C headers
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    # Blocking (D8): the generated headers are the musl fork's only view of the
    # minix.rs ABI, so a Rust-side change that produces uncompilable C must fail
    # in the slice that made it, not in 5.6 when the first C file appears.
    # `clang` needs no install step -- it ships on the GitHub runner images, and
    # kernel/build.rs already shells out to bare `clang` for the kernel's .S
    # files, so it is an existing hard build requirement (the green qemu-smoke
    # job on ubuntu-24.04-arm is the standing proof).
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@df4cb1c069e1874edd31b4311f1884172cec0e10 # v6.0.3
      - name: Install pinned toolchain
        run: rustup show
      - uses: Swatinem/rust-cache@e18b497796c12c097a38f9edb9d0641fb99eee32 # v2
